To install, see doc/install.html

Getting the code
----------------
Git (recommended):   git clone --depth 1 --single-branch --branch dist https://github.com/apc-aa/ActionApps.git apc-aa
                     update later with:  git pull --ff-only
Subversion (mirror): svn checkout https://svn.code.sf.net/p/apc-aa/svn/trunk apc-aa
                     update later with:  svn update

Both deliver the same runtime-only tree ("dist": vendor/ included, no composer needed on the
server); the SVN trunk is mirrored from the git dist branch after every change. Keep .git/ and
.svn/ out of the web server's reach, e.g. Apache:
    <DirectoryMatch "/\.(git|svn)"> Require all denied </DirectoryMatch>
Then create include/config.php from include/config.php.default (git installations; SVN
installations keep the shipped include/config.php shim and put their settings in
include/config.php3). After every update run the checks in admin -> AA -> Optimize
(service/sql_update.php) as before.

Developers work on the "main" branch (sources, tests, docs, dev/ build inputs):
    git clone https://github.com/apc-aa/ActionApps.git && cd ActionApps && composer install
dev/release/README.md describes how the dist branch and the SVN mirror are produced.
